[0m$ [0mgit commit -m "feat: Neon Raindrop Catcher - polished playable browser game

Implements Neon Raindrop Catcher as self-contained index.html with canvas-based gameplay.

Features:
- Glowing cup moves left/right with Arrow keys and A/D (smooth lerp 0.45, clamped, hold glide, pointer drag + touch hold buttons)
- Blue raindrops (r=9) catch for +10 score, red sparks (r=13) distinct larger star with black stroke and 1.5x faster fall (scales with level)
- Lives: 3 hearts, lost on missed blue or caught red; distinct feedback: hit shake 22 + red radial flash + hit-stop 6 frames vs miss shake 6 + cyan flash
- Score, level (every 100pts), increasing difficulty: spawnInterval 700->260, baseSpeed 2.2+(level*0.45), red ratio 22%->42%
- HUD with score/level/lives, neon arcade aesthetic (bloom via lighter composite, grid overlay boosted 0.45 opacity, CRT scanline, particles)
- Start/restart flow: start overlay, game over overlay with best score (localStorage), SPACE/Enter to start/restart, P/Esc to pause
- Responsive keyboard controls (preventDefault on arrows/space), touch drag, 60fps loop, WebAudio tones
- Self-contained single file with embedded CSS/JS, no external JS deps

Motivation: meets goal spec for small polished playable browser game.

Critic gap applied vs Pac-Man CE/Tetris Effect cabinet reference:
- Threat vs reward now distinct: size delta 4px, black keyline, additive bloom, speed cue 1.5x vs 1.18x, star spikes 14/6.5 vs blue teardrop

Verification:
- node --check /tmp/neon.js syntax ok
- curl http://localhost:8000/index.html 200 OK
- Playwright 1.62.1 chromium headless: canvas/context true, no JS errors, start overlay visible, game runs, drops spawn, keyboard no throw, flash element present
- Screenshots: final-start, final-gameplay, final-action, final-gameover (1280x900)

Chat-ID: ses_f9ffdaeebffezOdeaMZt30tZKL
